# Large binaries live in Git LFS. The rules are path-scoped rather than
# extension-scoped for `hardware/` because that tree is all binary source art
# (.drawio) and exports (.png/.jpg); the meshes are matched by extension so they
# stay in LFS wherever they sit.
#
# Anything the *website* renders must stay OUT of these paths: CI's checkout does
# not fetch LFS objects, so an LFS-backed image publishes as a ~130-byte text
# pointer served with an image MIME type — a 200 that renders broken. That is why
# the wiring photo the electronics page uses lives in `website/src/assets/`.
# `tests/doc_assets.test.mts` fails the build if that rule is broken again.
*.stl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
hardware/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
